// Canonic imitation with voice-level transformations applied per entry.
// Voice 1: subject. Voice 2 (enters at 4): subject in augmentation.
// Voice 3 (enters at 12): subject in diminution.
//
// !N places each voice in absolute time. Per-voice transformations like ||
// and > operate on the voice's content, independently of its entry offset.

subject = [0, 2, 4, 5, 4, 2]
subject
!4
subject || [2]
!12
subject || [1/2]
